## 🏗️ Architecture

### Design Patterns

1. **Repository Pattern**: Data access abstraction layer
   - `PlayerRepository`, `SettingsRepository`, `StatsRepository`, `WishesRepository`
   - Interface-based contracts in `services/repositories/interfaces.ts`
   - Implementations in `services/repositories/`

2. **Service Layer**: Business logic encapsulation
   - `AppService` handles app initialization, validation, stats
   - Services use repositories for data operations
   - Singleton instances exported from service files

3. **Custom Hooks**: Reusable logic composition
   - `useBottleSpin`: Bottle spinning logic with animation
   - `usePlayers`: Player management
   - `useSettings`: Settings management
   - Hooks return structured objects with state and handlers

4. **Separation of Concerns**
   ```
   Screen → Custom Hook → Service → Repository → Storage
     ↓
   Pure UI rendering, no business logic
   ```

### Project Structure

```
src/
├── components/           # Reusable UI components
│   ├── settings/        # Settings-specific components
│   ├── optimized/       # Performance-optimized components
│   ├── Bottle*.tsx      # Bottle variants (3D, Premium)
│   ├── Gradient*.tsx    # Gradient components
│   └── *Effects.tsx     # Visual effects (Confetti, Particles)
├── screens/             # Screen components (one per route)
│   ├── SplashScreen.tsx
│   ├── PlayersScreen.tsx
│   ├── ModeSelectionScreen.tsx
│   ├── WishesGameScreen.tsx
│   ├── DatingGameScreen.tsx
│   └── SettingsScreen.tsx
├── hooks/               # Custom React hooks
│   ├── useBottleSpin.ts
│   ├── usePlayers.ts
│   └── useSettings.ts
├── services/            # Business logic layer
│   ├── AppService.ts
│   └── repositories/    # Data access layer
│       ├── interfaces.ts
│       ├── PlayerRepositoryImpl.ts
│       ├── SettingsRepositoryImpl.ts
│       └── index.ts
├── types/               # TypeScript type definitions
│   └── index.ts
├── constants/           # App constants
│   ├── colors.ts
│   └── wishes.ts
└── utils/               # Utility functions
    ├── storage.ts
    └── performance.ts
```

